<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The git library's proofs run once more with the MinGit the toolchain pins (GITLIB1d): the parity classes (GitLibraryReads' shapes
  against git) and GitLibraryEndsTests, with that git the only one on the test host's PATH, so the product's starts and the
  fixtures' are both the pinned git's. The same classes run on the runner's git in git.process.runsettings; each leg compares the
  library with the git it runs.

  The switch is the one DAORIS_PINNED_GIT_LEG the test host reads as it loads (HostEnvironment). Where the pin cannot be had on a
  machine, every test of the leg is skipped saying why, never run on another git and passed. One class at a time: the library's classes
  assert its process-wide open count (GitLibrary.Open), which a second of them running beside moves, and the leg runs nothing else.

  The name ends in process.runsettings on purpose: the merge tool reads a gate run with such a file as a Process half, so this one
  keeps its trx and re-runs a failed test alone. Its filter is in the file for the same reason as the other's.
-->
<RunSettings>
  <RunConfiguration>
    <TestCaseFilter>Category=Process&amp;Parallel=Git&amp;(FullyQualifiedName~GitLibraryWalksTests|FullyQualifiedName~GitLibraryNamesTests|FullyQualifiedName~GitLibraryFormatsTests|FullyQualifiedName~GitLibraryRefsTests|FullyQualifiedName~GitLibraryCountedTests|FullyQualifiedName~GitLibraryEndsTests)</TestCaseFilter>
    <EnvironmentVariables>
      <DAORIS_PINNED_GIT_LEG>1</DAORIS_PINNED_GIT_LEG>
    </EnvironmentVariables>
  </RunConfiguration>
  <xUnit>
    <ParallelizeTestCollections>true</ParallelizeTestCollections>
    <MaxParallelThreads>1</MaxParallelThreads>
  </xUnit>
</RunSettings>
